                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "26610819",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198025498220",
                            "num_reviews": 22,
                            "playtime_forever": 552,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 552,
                            "last_played": 1479104243
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had more fun than I thought I would with this one. It plays like a stealth game, digging for treasure while trying to avoid being spotted and killed by the variety of spirits that haunt each graveyard. Some puzzles and mazes are thrown in, along with the optional goal of collecting keys from each stage that unlocks the final graveyard of the game.\n\nYou get a \"mission briefing\" at the beginning of each stage where the grave robber (YOU!) and his companion discuss the main score that you have to get at each graveyard to complete the level, along with some silly dialog that eventually leads to a bit of story later. You can go for the main goal and get out, or you can stick around and try to clear the entire graveyard for completion purposes and to get that special key I mentioned earlier, once you collect the map pieces from graves to find it.\n\nThere are a handful of enemy type in the game, and you'll get a tutorial on each one as you encounter them in the game. The Bride's my favorite enemy for her disturbing scream and determination to kill you once see spots you.  You also get a hard mode where enemies will randomly spawn as you remain in the level and you only get one life instead of three. I still have a few achievements to get, but the game took me around 4 to 5 hours to complete on Normal.",
